WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.202
With i18next, each
string gets a key,

2
00:00:04.202 --> 00:00:06.442
and every language
gets its own file.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:10.389
It renders messages
and selects plurals,

4
00:00:10.389 --> 00:00:13.326
and the translations come
from a separate service.

5
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.505
General Translation keeps your
copy inline and generates the

6
00:00:17.505 --> 00:00:18.433
translations.

7
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.622
Write the copy inline
inside a T component,

8
00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.096
with no keys to manage.

9
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:29.631
Then npx gt translate writes
every language before each build,

10
00:00:29.631 --> 00:00:31.952
with your JSX as context.

11
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:36.806
If you keep i18next, General
Translation can translate its

12
00:00:36.806 --> 00:00:38.001
existing catalogs.

13
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.192
Your team now ships
French with each release.
